---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **환불 규정.** (`/refund`)
 *
 * ── 왜 (2번 지시 13:3x) ───────────────────────────────────────
 * 「/terms · /refund 도 404 입니다」. 파는 조건 중 환불이다.
 *
 * ⛔ 6번 글을 베끼지 않는다. 뼈대(받기 전 전액 · 받은 뒤 없음 · 수치가 틀리면 전액)는
 *    디지털 자료면 어디나 같지만, **우리 쪽에만 있는 칸**이 하나 있다 —
 *    우리는 「이 표로는 답이 안 된다」를 **사기 전에** 말한다. 그 답이 늦어 산 것도 물린다.
 * ⛔ 「SeoulMarkets」·「백년지도」·「KLifeMap」이 여기 남으면 안 된다.
 * ⛔ 값을 안 적는다. 사장님 손이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../../consts';

const MAIL = 'parkintaek2@gmail.com';
const TITLE = 'Refund policy';
const DESC = 'Full refund before you download. None after, because it is a file — except when a '
  + 'figure is wrong, or when we failed to warn you the tables could not answer your question.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  url: 'https://www.kculturewire.com/refund',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'K Culture Wire', url: 'https://www.kculturewire.com' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: PUBLISHER.legalName, email: MAIL },
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/refund">
  <h1>Refund policy</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The data is a file, which shapes the rule. We keep it simple, and where we can we keep it in your
    favour.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Before you download — full refund</h2>
    <p>
      Change your mind before you have downloaded anything and we refund you <b>in full</b>, without
      asking why.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>After you download — no refund</h2>
    <p>
      Once the file is on your machine we cannot take it back, so a licence is
      <b> non-refundable after download</b>. That is the ordinary rule for digital data. The two
      exceptions below matter more than the rule.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If a figure is wrong — full refund, even after download</h2>
    <p>
      <b>If a number in a table you licensed is wrong, you get a full refund even after downloading
      it.</b> That is our mistake, not yours. We sell accuracy, so we carry the cost of missing it:
      report the error and we refund the licence, correct the figure, tell everyone else holding the
      file, and add the correction to
      <a href="/corrections"> the public record</a> with the cause it came from.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      We do this whether or not you ask for the money back. The record gets the correction either
      way — it is published before it is convenient.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If we failed to tell you it would not answer your question — full refund</h2>
    <p>
      This one is ours alone. Before anyone buys, we say <b>what these tables cannot answer</b> —
      the country lists carry no viewing hours, cast lists are incomplete, export figures run about
      eighteen months behind, and acts with no English Wikipedia article produce no row at all.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>If you told us what you were trying to measure and we did not warn you that the tables
      could not measure it, that is a refund</b>, download or no download. Selling someone the near
      miss is worse than selling them nothing, and we would rather pay for the error than keep the
      money.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to ask</h2>
    <p>
      Write to <a href={`mailto:${MAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('K Culture Wire — refund')}`}>{MAIL}</a>{' '}
      with what you bought and what went wrong. A person reads it and answers within a working day.
      There is no form, and you will not be asked to justify a refund we have already said you are
      owed.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {PUBLISHER.legalName}. Nothing here removes any right you have under Korean consumer law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="back">
    <a href="/terms">Terms of the licence</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/data">What is in the tables</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/corrections">Everything we have corrected</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span><a href="/">Front page</a>
  </p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.25; margin: 1.2rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 2.5rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  p { font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.75; margin: 0 0 .9rem; }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .back a { color: var(--muted); }
</style>
